{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Deliver me</b> — on account of the killing of Uriah." "<b>And the meaning of \"my tongue shall sing of Your righteousness\"</b> — for I am not a murderer and liable to death, for He did not command to kill him, only his thought was evil in placing him in a place of danger."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:37.534202578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}